--   The templates of the network are admissible at `q ^ f` (round six, `tok_edges`)
-- statement:
--   **The templates of the network are admissible at `q ^ f`.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6ILTok`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL.tok_edges (C : Bit.QHNet (ZMod 2) W T m) {q f Bb : ℕ} (hq : q.Prime)
--       (hqB : qBound C < q) (hf : 1 ≤ f) (hOK : C.EdgesOK (q ^ f))
--       (hBb : zsz ((((q ^ f + 1) ^ 3 : ℕ)) : ℤ) ≤ Bb) :
--       (∀ e ∈ C.edges, ∀ T' ∈ tplE e.E₁ ++ tplE e.E₂, TOK T' (q ^ f) Bb) ∧
--       (∀ e ∈ C.edges, ∀ i j, Nat.Coprime (e.E₁ i j).den (q ^ f) ∧
--         Nat.Coprime (e.E₂ i j).den (q ^ f))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, item language: the shift templates are admissible for large primes
--
--   `tok_edges`: for a prime `q` above the template constant `qBound C` and `f ≥ 1`, if the edges
--   are `EdgeOK` at `q ^ f`, then every shift template of every edge satisfies `TOK` at `q ^ f`, and
--   all matrix denominators are coprime to `q ^ f`.
--
